          "post_id": "1159910109929396",
          "url": "https://www.facebook.com/sugboph/posts/pfbid0ELbwJtEZszRo27WAN3fD38LY3DjMBHDQ3XhDzHPNJxdWZdPcNebAe42hJHPRCZibl",
          "timestamp": null,
          "message": "𝐁𝐈𝐑𝐇𝐄𝐍 𝐒𝐀 𝐒𝐈𝐌𝐀𝐋𝐀, 𝐄-𝐀𝐌𝐏𝐎 𝐌𝐎 𝐊𝐀𝐌𝐈! 🙏✨\n\nA place where faith, prayer, and hope come together. The Simala Shrine in Sibonga continues to draw pilgrims and visitors with its majestic castle-like architecture, sacred atmosphere, and deep devotion to the Virgin Mary.\n\nTake a quiet moment to pray, light a candle, write your intentions to Mama Mary, and simply pause amid the peaceful surroundings.\n\nWhether you’re visiting to seek guidance, give thanks, or simply reflect, Simala remains one of Cebu’s most meaningful pilgrimage destinations.\n\n📍 Monastery of the Holy Eucharist, Lindogon, Sibonga, Cebu\n🕊️ Open daily | Modest attire required\n\n📷 Contributed by Joey Argawanon | Want to get FEATURED on Sugbo.ph? Send us your Cebu photos, stories, or videos via m.me/SugboPH/.\n\n#SimalaShrine #Simala #Sibonga #SibongaCebu #PilgrimageDestination #FaithAndMiracles #CebuAttractions #SugboPH",
